PORTFOLIO WEBSITE CONTEXT DOC
============================

PROJECT SUMMARY
---------------
This is a single-page, interactive portfolio website built with plain HTML, CSS, and ES modules. It presents the owner's profile as a stylized space exploration experience: a cinematic splash portal opens into a canvas-based universe where three planets represent portfolio themes (experience, skills, projects). Clicking a planet opens a discovery modal with portfolio details.

PRIMARY GOAL
------------
Convert a conventional portfolio into an immersive, gamified visual experience that feels like a sci-fi exploration interface while still conveying professional information.

RUNTIME MODEL
-------------
- Entry point: index.html
- Core app bootstrap: js/main.js (AppEngine)
- Global portfolio content: js/data/content.js
- Rendering and interaction logic is split into modular engine/components files
- No build tool or framework is used; it runs directly in the browser as a static site

FILE HIERARCHY
--------------
root/
├── index.html
├── assets/
├── css/
│   ├── environment.css
│   ├── main.css
│   └── splash.css
└── js/
    ├── main.js
    ├── components/
    │   ├── compass.js
    │   ├── lavaPlanet.js
    │   ├── modal.js
    │   ├── neonPlanet.js
    │   ├── planet.js
    │   ├── portal.js
    │   └── verdantPlanet.js
    ├── data/
    │   └── content.js
    └── engine/
        ├── camera.js
        ├── events.js
        ├── physics.js
        ├── shading.js
        └── starfield.js

HOW THE SITE WORKS
------------------
1. index.html defines:
   - the splash portal section
   - the main universe canvas
   - the HUD and modal overlay containers
   - a module import to load AppEngine from js/main.js

2. On DOM ready, AppEngine.init() runs:
   - creates the portal animation
   - sets up event listeners
   - prepares the app for transition

3. Clicking the portal ring triggers transitionToUniverse():
   - the splash screen dissolves away
   - the universe becomes visible
   - the main engine starts: starfield, camera, planets, compass

4. The universe is interactive:
   - drag/scroll-like movement pans the camera across the scene
   - planets are rendered on canvas
   - clicking a planet opens a modal with content
   - the compass shows directional pointers when planets move off-screen

MAIN FILES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
------------------------------
- index.html
  - Page shell, metadata, CSS/JS includes, initial DOM structure

- js/main.js
  - Central orchestrator (AppEngine)
  - Initializes portal, modal, world, camera, and animation loop
  - Creates the three planet instances from content data
  - Handles universe transition and frame updates

- js/data/content.js
  - Contains window.PORTFOLIO_DATA, a structured manifest of the portfolio content, transcribed from DATA-README.md
  - Includes four sections: experience, skills, projects, contact
  - Each section's shape is tailored to its content (education/timeline, categorized stack, project cards, contact links) — no fabricated metrics

- js/components/portal.js
  - Draws the animated portal/splash effect using canvas particles
  - Creates the cinematic entry experience

- js/components/modal.js
  - Manages the discovery modal overlay
  - Injects content into the modal body based on clicked planet data
  - Supports Escape key and backdrop close

- js/components/compass.js
  - Displays arrow-like pointers to planets that are outside the viewport
  - Helps navigation in the large space

- js/components/planet.js
  - Base class for planets
  - Stores world coordinates, size, and shared update logic

- js/components/verdantPlanet.js
  - Renders the green/experience planet
  - Displays a verdant, earthlike visual style

- js/components/lavaPlanet.js
  - Renders the orange/skills planet
  - Uses a procedural texture generated by shading engine

- js/components/neonPlanet.js
  - Renders the purple/projects planet
  - Uses neon glow and ring effects

- js/engine/starfield.js
  - Generates and renders layered starfield background
  - Provides parallax depth through multiple star layers

- js/engine/camera.js
  - Handles panning and drag interactions
  - Updates the view offset with inertia/physics behavior

- js/engine/physics.js
  - Small physics helper for smoothing camera motion and drift

- js/engine/events.js
  - EventBus and InteractionManager for UI event coordination
  - Handles blur/focus and keyboard interactions

- js/engine/shading.js
  - Procedural surface generation used by the lava planet texture

CONTENT MODEL
-------------
The portfolio content is stored in window.PORTFOLIO_DATA and is structured as:
{
  experience: { id, category, title, summary, education: [...], timeline: [...] },
  skills: { id, category, title, description, stack: { Languages, Frontend, ... }, coreStrengths: [...] },
  projects: { id, category, title, description, items: [{ name, category, description, tech, highlights }] },
  contact: { id, category, title, description, links: [{ label, value, href }] }
}

This data is used to create the planets and to populate the modal content.

VISUAL DESIGN SYSTEM
--------------------
- Dark sci-fi / cosmic theme
- Typography uses Space Grotesk and Syncopate from Google Fonts
- Canvas-based rendering for the universe and portal
- CSS layers provide splash screen, HUD, modal styling, and animated transitions
- The site uses a custom neon/cyber aesthetic with glassmorphism-like panels

INTERACTION BEHAVIOR
--------------------
- Splash portal click: starts the transition into the universe
- Universe drag: pans camera view
- Planet click: opens modal with portfolio information
- Escape key: closes modal
- Window blur: pauses engine to save performance
- Compass pointers: show off-screen planets

IMPORTANT IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
------------------------------
- The site is static and browser-based; no backend or database is involved
- All portfolio data is client-side in JavaScript
- Most UI is generated dynamically at runtime rather than from static HTML
- The app depends on browser APIs such as Canvas, requestAnimationFrame, and DOM events
- The code is modular and uses ES modules with relative imports

CODEBASE PURPOSE MAP
--------------------
This section explains what each file is doing in the codebase, not just what it contains.

- index.html
  - Purpose: page bootstrap and shell. It defines the visible structure, loads CSS, wires the app entry, and provides the containers that the JavaScript engine populates at runtime.

- css/main.css
  - Purpose: global visual foundation. It establishes the design system, typography, color palette, shared UI styles, and base layout behavior.

- css/splash.css
  - Purpose: splash screen presentation. It controls the portal intro animation, portal ring visuals, text styling, and dissolve transition.

- css/environment.css
  - Purpose: universe and interaction styling. It defines the canvas scene, HUD, modal layout, compass pointers, and animation effects for the exploration experience.

- js/main.js
  - Purpose: application coordinator. It owns the startup sequence, creates the portal and world objects, wires events, and drives the main render loop.

- js/data/content.js
  - Purpose: content source of truth. It stores the portfolio narrative and metadata used by the planets and modal content.

- js/components/portal.js
  - Purpose: cinematic intro effect. It renders the animated portal using particle-based canvas drawing to create the “enter the nexus” experience.

- js/components/modal.js
  - Purpose: detail viewer. It turns planet interaction into a polished overlay that displays the selected portfolio topic in a richer format.

- js/components/compass.js
  - Purpose: navigation aid. It helps the user locate planets that have moved off-screen by rendering directional indicators.

- js/components/planet.js
  - Purpose: shared planet behavior. It centralizes common properties and logic used by all planet visual types.

- js/components/verdantPlanet.js
  - Purpose: experience-themed planet renderer. It visualizes the experience content as a green, organic-looking celestial body.

- js/components/lavaPlanet.js
  - Purpose: skills-themed planet renderer. It visualizes the technical stack/content with a procedural lava-and-ice surface aesthetic.

- js/components/neonPlanet.js
  - Purpose: projects-themed planet renderer. It visualizes the projects content with a neon, futuristic gas giant style.

- js/engine/starfield.js
  - Purpose: background layer. It draws the animated starfield that gives the universe depth and motion.

- js/engine/camera.js
  - Purpose: viewport controller. It manages panning, dragging, and camera offset updates for exploration.

- js/engine/physics.js
  - Purpose: motion smoothing. It adds inertia and drift behavior so camera movement feels fluid instead of abrupt.

- js/engine/events.js
  - Purpose: interaction abstraction. It provides reusable event handling and global input coordination such as Escape, blur/focus, and hover logic.

- js/engine/shading.js
  - Purpose: procedural texture generator. It creates the visual surface used by the lava-themed planet.

AGENT USAGE NOTES
-----------------
If an agent needs to understand or modify this site quickly, the most important files are:
1. index.html
2. js/main.js
3. js/data/content.js
4. js/components/modal.js
5. js/engine/camera.js
6. js/components/planet.js

These files contain the entry point, data source, interaction model, and core rendering architecture.
